                "summary": {
                    "type": "html",
                    "_value": "Vancomycin is used to treat colitis (inflammation of the intestine caused by certain bacteria) that may occur after taking an antibiotic. Vancomycin is in a class of medications called glycopeptide antibiotics. It works by killing bacteria in the intestines. Vancomycin will not kill bacteria in any other part of the body when taken by mouth. Antibiotics such as vancomycin will not work for colds, flu, or other viral infections. Taking antibiotics when they are not needed increases your risk of getting an infection later that resists antibiotic treatment."
                },
